# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "How to compute custom bounds for the latest version of Shaded lightcones"
msgstr "Cara menghitung bound kustom untuk versi terbaru Shaded lightcones"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "How to compute custom bounds"
msgstr "Cara menghitung bound kustom"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"addons/qiskit-addon-slc/guides/custom-bounds.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`compute_forward_bounds` and `compute_backward_bounds` are convenience wrappers. Both are built from\n"
"the same three pieces, which the public API exposes:\n"
msgstr ""
"`compute_forward_bounds` dan `compute_backward_bounds` adalah wrapper praktis. Keduanya dibangun dari\n"
"tiga bagian yang sama, yang diekspos oleh API publik:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A **norm function**, which bounds a single evolved Pauli error term\n"
msgstr "Sebuah **fungsi norm**, yang membatasi satu suku error Pauli yang sudah dievolusikan\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A **light cone**, which seeds what the error terms are evolved toward\n"
msgstr "Sebuah **light cone**, yang menentukan ke arah mana suku error dievolusikan\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`compute_bounds`, which iterates the circuit and distributes the per-term work\n"
msgstr "`compute_bounds`, yang mengiterasi circuit dan mendistribusikan pekerjaan per suku\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Assembling them yourself means you can bound something the wrappers don't cover. This guide works\n"
"through one case where that is worth doing: a **mirror circuit**, where the usual backward bound is\n"
"needlessly loose.\n"
msgstr ""
"Merakit ketiganya sendiri berarti kamu bisa membatasi sesuatu yang tidak dicakup wrapper. Panduan ini\n"
"membahas satu kasus yang layak dikerjakan begitu: **mirror circuit**, di mana bound backward yang biasa\n"
"terlalu longgar tanpa perlu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "What the wrappers actually do {#what-the-wrappers-actually-do}"
msgstr "Apa sebenarnya yang dilakukan wrapper {#what-the-wrappers-actually-do}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two wrappers differ in the three places listed above:\n"
msgstr "Kedua wrapper berbeda di tiga tempat yang tercantum di atas:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| | `compute_forward_bounds` | `compute_backward_bounds` |\n"
"| --- | --- | --- |\n"
"| circuit | as given | `remove_measure(circuit).inverse()` |\n"
"| norm function | `time_evolved_norm_forward`, against the observable | `time_evolved_norm_backward`, against the initial state |\n"
"| light cone | `LightCone.initialize_from_pauli`, seeded from the observable | `LightCone.initialize_from_measurements`, seeded from every active qubit |\n"
"| `backwards` | `False` | `True` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| | `compute_forward_bounds` | `compute_backward_bounds` |\n"
"| --- | --- | --- |\n"
"| circuit | sesuai input | `remove_measure(circuit).inverse()` |\n"
"| fungsi norm | `time_evolved_norm_forward`, terhadap observable | `time_evolved_norm_backward`, terhadap initial state |\n"
"| light cone | `LightCone.initialize_from_pauli`, diinisialisasi dari observable | `LightCone.initialize_from_measurements`, diinisialisasi dari setiap qubit aktif |\n"
"| `backwards` | `False` | `True` |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The forward bound asks *\"How much can this error change the observable I am about to measure?\"* and\n"
"answers it with the spectral norm of a commutator. The backward bound asks *\"How much can this error\n"
"change the state I started from?\"* and answers with a nuclear norm, taking that state to be the\n"
"all-zero state on every active qubit. They are different questions, and each is the right one for\n"
"errors in its own half of the circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bound forward bertanya *\"Seberapa besar error ini bisa mengubah observable yang akan saya ukur?\"* dan\n"
"menjawabnya dengan spectral norm dari sebuah commutator. Bound backward bertanya *\"Seberapa besar error ini bisa\n"
"mengubah state tempat saya memulai?\"* dan menjawabnya dengan nuclear norm, dengan menganggap state itu\n"
"adalah all-zero state pada setiap qubit aktif. Keduanya pertanyaan yang berbeda, dan masing-masing tepat untuk\n"
"error di setengah circuit-nya sendiri.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "The mirror circuit case {#the-mirror-circuit-case}"
msgstr "Kasus mirror circuit {#the-mirror-circuit-case}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A mirror circuit applies some unitary and then undoes it: $U^\\dagger U$. These appear whenever\n"
"the ideal outcome has to be known exactly (generally Loschmidt echoes, randomized benchmarking, and\n"
"verification experiments).\n"
msgstr ""
"Mirror circuit menerapkan suatu unitary lalu membatalkannya: $U^\\dagger U$. Ini muncul setiap kali\n"
"hasil idealnya harus diketahui dengan pasti (umumnya Loschmidt echo, randomized benchmarking, dan\n"
"eksperimen verifikasi).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Mirror circuits have a property the generic backward bound cannot exploit. Because the second half\n"
"is the inverse of the first, *evolving an error backward to the initial state* traverses the same\n"
"gates as *evolving it forward to the observable*. The two questions coincide, so the sharper\n"
"forward-style bound is valid for the backward direction too.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mirror circuit punya sifat yang tidak bisa dimanfaatkan oleh bound backward generik. Karena setengah kedua\n"
"adalah invers dari setengah pertama, *mengevolusikan error mundur ke initial state* melewati gate\n"
"yang sama dengan *mengevolusikannya maju ke observable*. Kedua pertanyaan itu bertemu, jadi bound\n"
"gaya forward yang lebih tajam valid juga untuk arah backward.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Assemble the custom bound {#assemble-the-custom-bound}"
msgstr "Merakit bound kustom {#assemble-the-custom-bound}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The recipe keeps what `compute_backward_bounds` does with the circuit (strip the measurements,\n"
"invert it, and iterate it with `backwards=True`) and substitutes the other two pieces: the forward\n"
"norm function, and a light cone seeded from the observable with `LightCone.initialize_from_pauli`,\n"
"exactly as `compute_forward_bounds` seeds its own. Each substitution is one line.\n"
msgstr ""
"Resepnya mempertahankan apa yang dilakukan `compute_backward_bounds` pada circuit (membuang pengukuran,\n"
"membalikkannya, dan mengiterasinya dengan `backwards=True`) dan mengganti dua bagian lainnya: fungsi\n"
"norm forward, serta light cone yang diinisialisasi dari observable dengan `LightCone.initialize_from_pauli`,\n"
"persis seperti `compute_forward_bounds` menginisialisasi miliknya. Setiap penggantian cukup satu baris.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "How much it gains {#how-much-it-gains}"
msgstr "Seberapa besar keuntungannya {#how-much-it-gains}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Comparing against the stock backward bound on the same circuit, summarized the same way as in the\n"
"[configuration guide](/addons/qiskit-addon-slc/guides/configuration-options): the mean bound and its standard deviation,\n"
"followed by the share of terms bounded by 0, with a bound computed in between, and left at the\n"
"trivial 2.0.\n"
msgstr ""
"Membandingkan dengan bound backward bawaan pada circuit yang sama, dirangkum dengan cara yang sama seperti di\n"
"[panduan konfigurasi](/addons/qiskit-addon-slc/guides/configuration-options): rata-rata bound dan standar deviasinya,\n"
"diikuti porsi suku yang di-bound 0, yang bound-nya dihitung di antaranya, dan yang dibiarkan di\n"
"nilai trivial 2.0.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The stock backward bound sits near the trivial value of 2.0, which carries almost no information. On\n"
"a mirror circuit, every error is \"close to the initial state\" in the sense that bound measures, so\n"
"it cannot discriminate between terms. The custom bound is several times tighter and bounds many of the terms by 0.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bound backward bawaan berada dekat nilai trivial 2.0, yang nyaris tidak memberi informasi. Pada\n"
"mirror circuit, setiap error \"dekat dengan initial state\" menurut ukuran bound itu, jadi\n"
"ia tidak bisa membedakan antar suku. Bound kustom beberapa kali lebih ketat dan membatasi banyak suku dengan 0.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To check the implementation, the two can be compared box by box. For every box, the\n"
"custom backward bound comes out **identical** to that same box's forward bound, up to rounding\n"
"error. Both bound the same error at the same point in the circuit, and on a mirror circuit the gates\n"
"after that point cancel to the inverse of the gates before it, so the two computations evaluate the\n"
"same quantity from opposite ends:\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk memeriksa implementasinya, keduanya bisa dibandingkan box demi box. Untuk setiap box,\n"
"bound backward kustom menghasilkan nilai yang **identik** dengan bound forward box yang sama, sampai\n"
"batas galat pembulatan. Keduanya membatasi error yang sama di titik yang sama dalam circuit, dan pada mirror circuit gate\n"
"setelah titik itu saling meniadakan menjadi invers dari gate sebelumnya, jadi kedua komputasi menghitung\n"
"besaran yang sama dari ujung yang berlawanan:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<div class=\"alert alert-info\">\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Note:** This equality is a property of the mirror structure, not of the technique. On a circuit\n"
"that is not self-inverting, the same substitution still runs but no longer computes a *valid* bound\n"
"for the backward direction: it answers the forward question about a circuit half where that\n"
"question does not apply. **Only use this when the second half of your circuit inverts the\n"
"first.**\n"
msgstr ""
"**Catatan:** Kesamaan ini adalah sifat dari struktur mirror, bukan dari tekniknya. Pada circuit yang\n"
"tidak self-inverting, penggantian yang sama tetap berjalan tetapi tidak lagi menghitung bound yang *valid*\n"
"untuk arah backward: ia menjawab pertanyaan forward tentang setengah circuit yang tidak cocok\n"
"untuk pertanyaan itu. **Pakai ini hanya kalau setengah kedua circuit-mu membalikkan\n"
"setengah pertama.**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "</div>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Feed it into the rest of the workflow {#feed-it-into-the-rest-of-the-workflow}"
msgstr "Masukkan ke sisa alur kerja {#feed-it-into-the-rest-of-the-workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The result is an ordinary `Bounds` dictionary, so everything that follows is unchanged.\n"
msgstr "Hasilnya adalah dictionary `Bounds` biasa, jadi semua yang menyusul tidak berubah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"On a mirror circuit there is also no reason to compute either bound for the whole circuit. The\n"
"forward bounds are only needed for the boxes of $U^\\dagger$, counted from the end, and the backward\n"
"bounds only for the boxes of $U$, counted from the start. `max_num_boxes` therefore limits each of\n"
"them to half of the noisy boxes, and `merge_bounds` joins the two halves.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pada mirror circuit juga tidak ada alasan untuk menghitung salah satu bound untuk seluruh circuit. Bound\n"
"forward hanya dibutuhkan untuk box dari $U^\\dagger$, dihitung dari akhir, dan bound backward\n"
"hanya untuk box dari $U$, dihitung dari awal. Karena itu `max_num_boxes` membatasi masing-masing\n"
"ke setengah dari box yang noisy, dan `merge_bounds` menggabungkan kedua setengahnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is how the bounds are used in practice, and it means the box-for-box comparison above is no\n"
"longer available: it needs both bounds for every box. It is a check of the implementation for this guide, not workflow step.\n"
msgstr ""
"Beginilah bound dipakai dalam praktik, dan itu berarti perbandingan box-demi-box di atas tidak\n"
"lagi tersedia: perbandingan itu butuh kedua bound untuk setiap box. Itu hanya pemeriksaan implementasi untuk panduan ini, bukan langkah alur kerja.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With the stock backward bounds, the sampling overhead is far larger. `merge_bounds` uses the\n"
"backward bounds up to one switch point in the circuit and the forward bounds from there on,\n"
"choosing the point that minimizes the total bias. With each bound computed for one half, that point\n"
"falls in the middle of the circuit, so the boxes of $U$ are covered by backward bounds alone. The\n"
"stock backward bound is close to the trivial 2.0 there, which drives the overhead up. The custom\n"
"one is as tight as the forward bound would have been, so the overhead matches that of the complete\n"
"forward bounds.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dengan bound backward bawaan, sampling overhead jauh lebih besar. `merge_bounds` memakai\n"
"bound backward sampai satu titik peralihan di circuit dan bound forward sesudahnya,\n"
"memilih titik yang meminimalkan total bias. Dengan tiap bound dihitung untuk satu setengah, titik itu\n"
"jatuh di tengah circuit, jadi box dari $U$ hanya dicakup oleh bound backward. Bound backward\n"
"bawaan di sana dekat dengan 2.0 yang trivial, yang mendorong overhead naik. Yang kustom\n"
"sama ketatnya dengan bound forward, jadi overhead-nya sama dengan overhead bound forward\n"
"lengkap.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"That raises the obvious question of why to bother, when the complete forward bounds alone give the\n"
"same result. The answer is cost. A forward bound for a box early in the circuit evolves its error\n"
"through the rest of $U$ and then all of $U^\\dagger$, which is the longest and widest evolution in\n"
"the circuit. The evolved operator can grow exponentially in the number of non-Clifford gates\n"
"it passes through, and computing the commutator's spectral norm gets exponentially more expensive as\n"
"the light cone widens. In the half-and-half approach, no error is evolved through more than half of\n"
"the circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Itu memunculkan pertanyaan yang jelas: kenapa repot-repot, kalau bound forward lengkap saja sudah memberi\n"
"hasil yang sama. Jawabannya adalah biaya. Bound forward untuk box di awal circuit mengevolusikan error-nya\n"
"melalui sisa $U$ lalu seluruh $U^\\dagger$, yang merupakan evolusi terpanjang dan terlebar di\n"
"circuit. Operator yang dievolusikan bisa tumbuh secara eksponensial terhadap jumlah gate non-Clifford\n"
"yang dilaluinya, dan menghitung spectral norm commutator menjadi eksponensial lebih mahal seiring\n"
"melebarnya light cone. Dengan pendekatan setengah-setengah, tidak ada error yang dievolusikan melewati lebih dari separuh\n"
"circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The saving therefore grows with the circuit depth. More importantly, the complete forward\n"
"bounds stop being computable long before the halfway ones do. Once the evolutions of the early\n"
"boxes exceed `evolution_max_terms` or `eigval_max_qubits`, their bounds are truncated or fall back\n"
"to the triangle inequality, and eventually they cost too much to compute. Wherever that point\n"
"lies, the half-and-half approach only needs it to fall somewhere in the first half of the circuit.\n"
"The forward bounds have to reach no further than the middle, and on a mirror circuit, the backward\n"
"bounds for the boxes of $U$ evolve their errors back to the start through as much of the\n"
"circuit as the forward bounds for the matching boxes of $U^\\dagger$ do to the end, so they run out\n"
"at the same depth.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jadi penghematannya bertambah seiring kedalaman circuit. Yang lebih penting, bound forward\n"
"lengkap berhenti bisa dihitung jauh sebelum yang setengahnya. Begitu evolusi box\n"
"awal melampaui `evolution_max_terms` atau `eigval_max_qubits`, bound-nya terpotong atau jatuh kembali\n"
"ke pertidaksamaan segitiga, dan akhirnya terlalu mahal untuk dihitung. Di mana pun titik itu\n"
"berada, pendekatan setengah-setengah hanya butuh titik itu jatuh di suatu tempat di separuh pertama circuit.\n"
"Bound forward tidak perlu menjangkau lebih jauh dari tengah, dan pada mirror circuit, bound\n"
"backward untuk box dari $U$ mengevolusikan error mundur ke awal melalui circuit sebanyak\n"
"yang dilalui bound forward untuk box padanan dari $U^\\dagger$ ke akhir, jadi keduanya kehabisan tenaga\n"
"pada kedalaman yang sama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Note:** Why compute backward bounds for the boxes of $U$, when the forward bounds of the\n"
"boxes of $U^\\dagger$ look like they should hold the same numbers? Because the boxes are not mirror\n"
"images of each other. Each box injects its noise on one side of its gates, and the inverse layers of\n"
"$U^\\dagger$ are separate boxes with noise models of their own, so the box that mirrors a box of $U$\n"
"sees its errors at a different point in the circuit. Therefore, their bounds only partly agree, and\n"
"the bounds for the boxes of $U$ have to be computed for those boxes.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Catatan:** Kenapa menghitung bound backward untuk box dari $U$, padahal bound forward dari\n"
"box $U^\\dagger$ tampaknya harus punya angka yang sama? Karena box-nya bukan bayangan cermin satu\n"
"sama lain. Setiap box menyuntikkan noise-nya di satu sisi gate-nya, dan layer invers dari\n"
"$U^\\dagger$ adalah box terpisah dengan model noise sendiri, jadi box yang mencerminkan box dari $U$\n"
"melihat error-nya di titik yang berbeda dalam circuit. Karena itu, bound keduanya hanya sebagian cocok, dan\n"
"bound untuk box dari $U$ harus dihitung untuk box-box tersebut.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Writing other custom bounds {#writing-other-custom-bounds}"
msgstr "Menulis bound kustom lainnya {#writing-other-custom-bounds}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The same three substitutions cover other cases:\n"
msgstr "Tiga penggantian yang sama mencakup kasus lain:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**A different norm.** `time_evolved_norm_forward` accepts `comm_norm_order`; passing anything\n"
"other than `2` skips the eigensolver and computes that norm directly.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Norm yang berbeda.** `time_evolved_norm_forward` menerima `comm_norm_order`; memberi nilai selain\n"
"`2` melewati eigensolver dan menghitung norm itu secara langsung.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**A different light cone.** `LightCone.initialize_from_pauli` seeds a light cone from any Pauli,\n"
"and the `LightCone` constructor takes the qubits to track and the operations seeding it, so a\n"
"bound can be computed against any operator you can express that way.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Light cone yang berbeda.** `LightCone.initialize_from_pauli` menginisialisasi light cone dari Pauli apa pun,\n"
"dan constructor `LightCone` menerima qubit yang dilacak dan operasi yang menginisialisasinya, jadi\n"
"bound bisa dihitung terhadap operator apa pun yang bisa kamu ekspresikan dengan cara itu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**A different norm function entirely.** `compute_bounds` only requires a callable: taking a\n"
"`Pauli` and `RotationGates` and returning a `CommutatorBounds`. Anything satisfying that signature\n"
"works, including a closed-form bound specific to your circuit family.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Fungsi norm yang sama sekali berbeda.** `compute_bounds` hanya mensyaratkan sebuah callable: yang menerima\n"
"`Pauli` dan `RotationGates` dan mengembalikan `CommutatorBounds`. Apa pun yang memenuhi signature itu\n"
"bisa dipakai, termasuk bound closed-form yang spesifik untuk keluarga circuit-mu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Whatever you substitute, you must prove that the result is a genuine upper bound.\n"
"Understating an error term's effect does not produce a visible failure. It produces an expectation\n"
"value that is quietly wrong, because the term will have been dropped from the mitigated noise model.\n"
msgstr ""
"Apa pun yang kamu gantikan, kamu harus membuktikan bahwa hasilnya benar-benar upper bound.\n"
"Meremehkan pengaruh suku error tidak menimbulkan kegagalan yang terlihat. Hasilnya adalah expectation\n"
"value yang diam-diam salah, karena suku itu akan terbuang dari model noise yang dimitigasi.\n"
